Package: patrone-default-apps
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, chromium-browser
Recommends: patrone-file-manager, patrone-terminal, patrone-unpack
Description: Patrone Linux's default apps
 Makes Chromium the default web browser and puts it in the favorites in place
 of Firefox, along with Patrone Terminal. Folders open in Patrone File
 Manager, which takes Ubuntu's Files' place in the favorites, and archives,
 .deb packages and Flatpak files in Patrone Unpack. Chromium comes from
 Canonical's snap, which keeps it up to date. Users' own choices still win.
